[66,2,0,1851,"Saint-Savin","Gustave Le Gray photographed this old abbey church with its tall spire for the French government, which sent photographers to record historic buildings that needed repair. It was one of the first photo projects for protecting heritage.","How tall is the spire compared with the church?"],
[68,4,0,1848,"Rue Royale After the Barricades","In February 1848, Parisians built barricades in the streets and overthrew their king. Bayard photographed the Rue Royale just after the fighting, with paving stones torn up and a few barricades left.","What do you think happened here a few days before?"],
[69,1,0,1848,"A View of Niagara","Platt Babbitt was the official photographer at Niagara Falls and sold daguerreotypes to tourists. It is one of the earliest photographs of the great waterfall.","What sounds do you imagine you would hear here?"],
